
Install Petsc into the home directory using the following steps:


Add the following to .bashrc:

    export PETSC_DIR=/home/simon/petsc
    export PETSC_ARCH=linux-gnu-optimized

Configure and install petsc:

    ./configure PETSC_ARCH=linux-gnu-optimized --with-precision=double --with-scalar-type=complex  --with-fc=0 --with-debugging=0 COPTFLAGS='-O3 -march=native -mtune=native'
    make all check


Install Slepcs into the home directory using the following steps:

     ./configure
     make SLEPC_DIR=/home/simon/slepc-3.19.1 PETSC_DIR=/home/simon/petsc PETSC_ARCH=linux-gnu-optimized




To compile the program with the Slepc libs use the following  makefile:

include ${SLEPC_DIR}/lib/slepc/conf/slepc_common





To use the perl wrapper script 'run.pl'
install libmoosex-app-perl (on Debian based distros).